TI  - Case Report of Neonatal Bronchoesophageal Fistula With Esophageal Atresia.
PG  - e02081
LID - 10.1213/XAA.0000000000002081 [doi]
AB  - We report a rare case of congenital esophageal atresia (EA) associated with 
      bronchoesophageal fistula (BEF) identified intraoperatively in a neonate 
      initially presumed to have tracheoesophageal fistula (TEF). Intraoperative 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy facilitated the localization and confirmation of the 
      fistula prior to surgical ligation. The BEF was ligated via open thoracotomy. 
      Esophageal repair was deferred due to a long gap between proximal and distal 
      esophagus pouches. This case underscores the importance of comprehensive airway 
      evaluation in neonates with suspected TEF/EA.
