TI  - A Life-Threatening Cause of Stridor, Primary Tracheal Actinomycosis.
PG  - e01952025
LID - S0037-86822026000101801 [pii]
LID - 10.1590/0037-8682-0195-2025 [doi]
LID - e0195-2025
AB  - Actinomycosis is a chronic, suppurative infection caused by Actinomyces israelii, 
      an anaerobic bacterium that is part of the normal oral flora. A 47-year-old woman 
      presented to the clinic with dyspnea and sore throat. Computed tomography(CT) 
      revealed thickening of the proximal tracheal lumen and airway narrowing. 
      Pathological examination of biopsy specimens obtained by rigid bronchoscopy 
      revealed periodic acid-Schiff (PAS)(+) bacterial colonization with filamentous 
      bacilli, consistent with Actinomyces. This report describes an uncommon 
      presentation of tracheal actinomycosis in which tracheal dilatation was performed 
      for both diagnostic sampling and therapeutic management of tracheal stenosis.
