TI  - [Prioritizing interventional diagnosis and treatment for tracheobronchial 
      tuberculosis: paradigm shift and clinical practice enhancement based on the 2025 
      guidelines].
PG  - 496-499
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112147-20250901-00532 [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchial tuberculosis (TBTB) is a key cause of long-term lung function 
      impairment and diminished quality of life in pulmonary tuberculosis patients. 
      Although the Guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of tracheobronchial 
      tuberculosis (2025 Edition) systematically establishes a new diagnosis and 
      treatment framework, prevalent issues in clinical practice-including insufficient 
      awareness, delayed diagnosis, and non-standardized technical application-severely 
      constrain the improvement of TBTB treatment outcomes. This article aims to 
      integrate the core updates of the new guidelines with the latest international 
      research advances to analyze the severe challenges currently faced in TBTB 
      diagnosis and treatment. It advocates for the foundational role of bronchoscopic 
      interventional technology in the comprehensive management of the disease and 
      calls on clinicians to restructure clinical practice with the philosophy of 
      "early intervention, precise classification, and multidisciplinary collaboration" 
      to meaningfully improve the prevention and management of TBTB.
FAU - Wang, H W
