TI  - Pulmonary Langerhans Cell Histiocytosis Presenting as Multiple Obstructing 
      Bronchial Lesions and Pulmonary Masses.
PG  - e70194
LID - 10.1111/crj.70194 [doi]
LID - e70194
AB  - Pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis is a rare lung disease, which was 
      previously classified as interstitial lung disease but is now classified as a 
      myeloid neoplasm. The obstructing tracheobronchial lesion or mass may rarely be 
      the manifestation of the disease. We describe a case of pulmonary Langerhans cell 
      histiocytosis presenting as multiple obstructing bronchial lesions and pulmonary 
      masses in a 36-year-old man. This case represents an extremely rare manifestation 
      of pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis.
