TI  - Systemic sarcoidosis in a TB-endemic region: diagnostic role of linear 
      endobronchial ultrasound mediastinal lymph node cryobiopsy and stepwise 
      management approach.
LID - e270697 [pii]
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2025-270697 [doi]
AB  - Sarcoidosis is a multisystem granulomatous disease that can mimic tuberculosis 
      (TB) or lymphoma, particularly in endemic regions. We report a man in his late 
      50s with chronic cough, weight loss and systemic features whose CT showed 
      mediastinal and abdominal lymphadenopathy with splenic lesions. Histology from 
      endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial cryobiopsy revealed non-caseating 
      granulomas, confirming sarcoidosis and excluding TB and malignancy. He responded 
      well to corticosteroids with methotrexate as a steroid-sparing agent. This case 
      emphasises the diagnostic challenge of sarcoidosis in TB-endemic regions and 
      highlights the added value of cryobiopsy in obtaining adequate tissue for 
      diagnosis.
