TI  - Combination of Photodynamic and Bronchoscopic Intervention With Radiation Therapy 
      in Treating Pulmonary Pleomorphic Sarcoma: A Case Report.
PG  - e70129
LID - 10.1111/crj.70129 [doi]
LID - e70129
AB  - Primary pulmonary synovial sarcoma (PPSS) is a rare and challenging malignancy in 
      terms of diagnosis and treatment. We narrated a case of PPSS treated innovatively 
      by integrating photodynamic therapy (PDT) and localized radiation, overcoming 
      diagnostic and treatment challenges associated with PPSS. The combination 
      significantly improved clinical symptoms and patient survival. The case sheds 
      light on a promising therapeutic strategy, augmenting the treatment discourse for 
      PPSS and potentially guiding future clinical practices in managing this rare 
      malignancy.
