TI  - Diagnosis of right upper lobe lesion using the SUKEDACHI balloon with 
      thin-bronchoscope to facilitate close-to-lesion transbronchial biopsy: Novel 
      bronchoscopic technique.
PG  - 853-856
LID - S2212-5345(25)00104-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.resinv.2025.07.003 [doi]
AB  - We report the first clinical use of a single-use bronchial dilatation catheter 
      (SUKEDACHI) with a thin bronchoscope to diagnose a peripheral upper lobe lung 
      lesion. In a man in his 70s, a part-solid nodule in the right upper lobe was 
      difficult to reach using standard techniques. Balloon-assisted bronchial 
      dilatation enabled advancement of the bronchoscope close to the lesion, allowing 
      biopsy with standard forceps. Histopathology confirmed lung adenocarcinoma. This 
      case highlights the potential of new technique to facilitate close-to-the-lesion 
      access and improve diagnostic yield for peripheral pulmonary lesions.
