TI  - Modification of the Murphy's Eye of a Single-Lumen Endotracheal Tube to 
      Facilitate One-Lung Ventilation in a Child Having a Robotic Sleeve Resection of 
      the Left Bronchus.
PG  - e01985
LID - 10.1213/XAA.0000000000001985 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial intubation with a single-lumen endotracheal tube (ETT) is a 
      technique to provide one-lung ventilation in small children. The shorter length 
      of the right mainstem bronchus poses challenges while placing an ETT on the right 
      side. Although the recommendation is to position the Murphy's eye of an ETT to 
      approximate with the right upper lobe bronchus orifice, this allows only a small 
      segment of the ETT to be placed in the bronchus, with a risk for tube 
      dislodgement. A modification of elongating the Murphy's eye can enable the tube 
      to be placed more distally while maintaining ventilation to the right upper lobe.
