TI  - Feasibility of the lung base-flip approach for complex segmentectomy of the lower 
      lobe.
LID - 10.1510/mmcts.2024.132 [doi]
AB  - Segmentectomies of the lung base, such as S9, S10 or S9+S10, present technical 
      difficulties because they do not connect directly to the interlobar fissure. The 
      lung base-flip approach offers easier access to the individual segmental vessels 
      and bronchi. We performed a segmentectomy of the lung base using this approach. 
      To identify the corresponding vessels and bronchi, flipped three-dimensional 
      chest computed tomography images and intraoperative bronchoscopy are essential.
