TI  - [Atelectasis caused by mucus stasis].
LID - D8265 [pii]
AB  - A 58-year-old female presented at the emergency department with dyspnea. 
      Laboratory and X-ray analyses showed eosinophilia and a partial atelectasis of 
      the left lung, respectively. Bronchoscopy demonstrated mucus plugs. Following 
      bronchoscopy, intubation was needed because of acute respiratory failure. 
      Biochemical and microbial tests confirmed the diagnosis allergic bronchopulmonary 
      aspergillosis. Complete recovery was achieved after treatment with prednisone and 
      voriconazole.
