TI  - Pulmonary Sclerosing Pneumocytoma: A Case Revealed During 8-year of Follow-up 
      with CT Imaging.
PG  - 893-897
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.3956-24 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary sclerosing pneumocytoma (PSP) is a rare, benign tumor. Given the 
      challenges of a bronchoscopic diagnosis, surgery is performed during the early 
      stages of the disease. Therefore, little is known about the growth pattern of 
      PSP. This case of PSP was not diagnosed despite bronchoscopy, resulting in lung 
      resection eight years after the anomaly was first identified on computed 
      tomography (CT). This report compares the long-term follow-up of CT and 
      pathological findings and discusses the difficulty in making a diagnosis using a 
      bronchoscopic forceps biopsy to aid in future PSP diagnoses and treatment 
      planning.
